WEBVTT

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.960
Well? How'd it go?

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:26.610
He dumped me.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:29.210
What? What happened?

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:31.490
He dumped me.

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:32.970
Not the other way around?

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:35.960
Nope. Go ahead, feel 
free to joke about it.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:37.750
Nah, that's okay...

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:43.450
Just the fact that we're 
here is weird enough.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.480
If he didn't want to 
come, he shouldn't have.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.800
Same goes for you guys, of course.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:49.540
We wouldn't have come 
if we didn't want to.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:50.480
Yeah.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:55.480
I'm going to look after him, 
then take him back home.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.240
You guys can head back first.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:00:59.740
You okay?

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:12.000
Yeah. I'll see you at school.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:19.470
Moyashimon

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:19.470
Returns

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:50.220
Sorry to bring you out here 
at this hour, Grandpa.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.930
No need for anyone to apologize.

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:05.830
Even if nobody believes 
those microbes spoke to us,

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:07.790
it was all true.

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:10.100
It really was cold in the winery,

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.920
and our family was in pieces.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:17.960
Everyone in our family is 
so stubborn, including me,

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.530
that we hate bending our own will,

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:21.180
or letting anyone else bend it.

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:25.770
My brother and I decided we wouldn't 
interfere until Dad could make

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:27.620
wine he was proud of.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:29.450
Then my brother went to Paris,

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:32.010
and I decided to venture out 
on my own someday, too.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:34.520
But that was all a lie.

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:39.360
I... no, both of us wanted 
to stay here and make wine.

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:43.180
If I'm getting in everyone's 
way, I apologize.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.700
It's true that I can't even drink wine.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:48.620
Maybe it would be best to 
leave everything to you.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:52.250
Is that what you wanted 
to say to me, Marie?

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:54.410
No, Dad.

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:58.880
But... this might upset you again...

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:02.500
No, I have nothing more 
to hide from you.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:04.390
I want to hear it.

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:17.650
It's the one I showed you in the cave.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:19.530
Both of you, try it.

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:22.980
Drink, Nico.

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:26.770
We won't get anywhere if 
we don't listen to Marie.

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:35.540
Honestly, even one sip 
gives me a headache...

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:40.240
It's not Pinot... a sweet champagne?

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:42.920
Huh?

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:46.120
The Paul Giraud family is noted for

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:48.140
producing cognac in Grande Champagne.

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:50.510
This is an ingredient in their cognac,

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:53.740
a popular product made 
from Ugni Blanc grapes,

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:55.020
sparkling grape juice.

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:57.810
Sparkling grape juice?

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:00.540
The Paul Giraud family

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:03.670
makes the juice carefully 
with the first

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.710
cognac grapes in the harvest.

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:09.330
A winery making an earnest 
effort to make juice?

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:12.120
The Pinot Noir in our vineyards are

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.830
delicious grapes with high 
sugar content, right?

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:18.070
Are you saying that 
you'll make the wine,

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:21.090
so your father should make 
juice from the Pinot Noir?

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:23.270
You're not ready for that.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:27.340
Wine isn't so forgiving that 
you could make it on your own.

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:30.130
That's why I want us 
to do this together!

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:32.850
Grandpa, I want you to 
revoke your retirement.

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:37.120
I mean, why would you retire 
when you're so active?

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:39.600
We're not going to let you 
get away with goofing off

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:41.210
while we do all the work!

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:44.680
If you're going to say 
I'm too optimistic

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:47.580
and my hands are too 
soft to make wine,

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.290
all you have to do is show me the ropes,

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:50.850
and none of that will matter.

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:53.580
I've been thinking for some time...

00:05:54.590 --> 00:05:59.540
About why we make these rich, 
sweet, and delicious Pinot Noir grapes

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:02.450
into such a harsh, sour drink.

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:04.820
Juice, eh?

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:06.990
So this is really possible.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:09.280
Dad...

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:11.780
Grape juice made from the best

00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:14.640
Pinot Noir grapes in 
the Burgundy domaine...

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:18.310
This just might catch 
everyone's interest, Marie,

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:21.150
not only the ones who 
can't drink alcohol.

00:06:24.010 --> 00:06:25.910
The white grapes planted by the great

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:27.780
Charlemagne, who hated red wine,

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:30.540
became the magnificent 
white wine of Burgundy.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:32.390
This is a chance for a man like me,

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:33.930
who can't drink alcohol,

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:36.880
to be selfish like Charlemagne!

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:39.160
Thank you.

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:42.260
It's a wonderful proposal, Marie.

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:11.560
Our work is done, Marie.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:12.630
What about you?

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:15.700
A miracle happened at 
our house yesterday.

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:18.080
But you wouldn't believe me 
if I told you, so I won't.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:18.950
Oh?

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:20.450
Is that right?

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:24.080
Hasegawa-san wanted us to thank you.

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:26.610
Really? I'm glad to hear it.

00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:32.060
Our family was chosen to reap

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:34.730
the bounty of this chosen 
land of Côte-d'Or,

00:07:34.730 --> 00:07:38.560
the miracle grapes we call 
Pinot Noir a jus Blanc.

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:42.620
Well, Grandpa still needs 
a little more convincing,

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:43.600
but it'll be okay.

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:46.860
Hey, Marie, would you 
come look at this vine?

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:52.960
I'll be back. Wait here, okay?

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:54.370
We'll celebrate tonight!

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:04.100
Côte-d'Or... Golden Hillside, huh?

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:05.990
It's a great name.

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:06.590
Sure is.

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:07.440
Yep.

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:18.130
Natural cheese is a 
fermented product

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:21.020
made with milk from animals such 
as cows, goats, and sheep.

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:23.600
It's a living product 
whose flavor changes

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:26.020
over time through the work of microbes.

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:27.950
Processed cheese, on the other hand,

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:27.950
Haruka?

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:30.020
Haruka, come back!

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:30.410
is made by processing natural cheese.

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:32.430
Isn't Haruka back yet?

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:32.510
It was originally made 
with shelf life in mind,

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:34.020
so the work of the microbes was

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:35.530
stopped through application of heat.

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:35.530
Where's Haruka?

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:38.560
In France, they say you can't 
have bread without cheese,

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:41.540
and you can't have bread 
and cheese without wine.

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:43.460
It's a truly superb fermented product

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:46.000
with close ties to the French diet.

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:49.130
So, Misato-kun, Kawahama-kun,

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:51.010
what kind of cheese did you buy for me?

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:53.570
We totally forgot.

00:08:56.850 --> 00:08:59.030
Poor Professor.

00:08:59.710 --> 00:09:01.020
And where's Sawaki-kun?

00:09:02.550 --> 00:09:04.520
He must be wiped out.

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:06.270
Now then, let's review!

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:09.440
In France, "hello" is "bonjour."

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:12.030
"Goodbye" is "au revoir." Go!

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:16.760
Bonjour! Au revoir!

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.760
So anyway, even in France,

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:19.680
Tadayasu didn't really do anything.

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:22.830
We microbes did lots of 
good things, though!

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:22.750
Oui, oui.

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:26.540
Would you just let me 
sleep a little longer?

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:28.080
Hiyoshi Liquor Store

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:32.550
Yuuki
Liquor

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:35.300
Okay, I'm off.

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:37.800
Yes, go enjoy yourself now and then.

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:39.060
Yeah.

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:41.310
I haven't seen everyone in so long.

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:45.720
Not everyone is here,

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:47.310
but at any rate, job well done.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:50.140
Is Sawaki still sleeping?

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:53.000
I told him to come here 
when he got back...

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:55.470
Oh, it's Yuuki-kun.

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:59.880
He's on his way here 
with Sawaki-kun now.

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:03.330
Oh, and thank you for the souvenir.

00:10:03.590 --> 00:10:05.990
No problem. The wine was free,

00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:08.710
so the three of us got as 
much as we could bring back.

00:10:09.090 --> 00:10:12.290
Haruka-san won't reply to my text...

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:15.090
Why didn't she come back with you?

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:18.380
Rich people have their 
own problems, I guess.

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:20.090
I'm sure she'll be back soon enough.

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:23.350
Hey, welcome back.

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:26.480
What? It's not just Mutou?

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:28.800
Welcome home!

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:30.960
What's with you?!

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:35.110
Thank goodness... I'm so glad!

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:38.130
I thought I'd never see you again!

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:40.990
You guys are going way overboard...

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:42.630
Haruka-san!

00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:44.550
Are you gonna make Hasegawa drink?

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:47.870
This is a bar, you know.

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:53.590
You're still sleepy?

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:54.850
Yeah...

00:10:54.850 --> 00:10:57.880
The plane was full of microbes, 
so I couldn't sleep.

00:10:58.320 --> 00:11:00.500
You didn't get a stomachache?

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:03.040
Now that you mention it, I didn't.

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:06.310
You've grown up.

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:07.850
What do you mean by that?

00:11:10.030 --> 00:11:11.310
Welcome back.

00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:14.020
Meeting up here? How nice.

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:15.540
Good to be back.

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:17.120
Good evening.

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:19.090
The bar's reserved for 
you guys tonight,

00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:20.480
so take your time.

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:21.800
The others are inside.

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:22.530
Thanks.

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:24.370
Are you serious?!

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:26.880
But, but, but, but!

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:29.060
She didn't take a bath? So then...

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:32.330
She was all muddy, 
but she still didn't take a bath?!

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:34.080
Right! Isn't that crazy?

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:35.240
Isn't that awful?

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:36.530
It wasn't like that.

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:38.440
Stop it, Kawahama!

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:40.560
I told you, nothing 
happened between us!

00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:40.560
Sawaki-kun, welcome.

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:42.180
So did you get to stir anything up?

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:44.640
No, it was as normal as normal gets.

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:45.470
What?

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:46.060
Nothing...

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:49.220
Still, it's great to see 
so many new couples forming

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:50.630
in the Itsuki seminar, huh?

00:11:50.630 --> 00:11:53.300
Why are you talking like 
that, too? Quit it.

00:11:53.860 --> 00:11:55.780
You look cute, Yuuki.

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:57.250
Do you ever wear white?

00:11:57.250 --> 00:11:57.940
Huh?

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:00.370
Sawaki likes white.

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:01.580
You do?

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:03.250
Uh... well...

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:05.690
If you'd say something, 
I'd wear white, too.

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:07.200
You don't have to force yourself...

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:10.850
That's right, Sawaki! 
What happened with Marie?

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:12.280
Oh yeah! That happened, too!

00:12:12.280 --> 00:12:13.710
I'm the only one who got no action!

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:15.100
Marie?

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:17.390
A French girl who looked like you.

00:12:22.390 --> 00:12:24.150
S-Sorry, Sawaki!

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:26.440
Even I don't know what came over me...

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:40.320
You guys are hilarious.

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:42.700
Have you...

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:44.530
...changed, Hasegawa-san?

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:46.010
Have I?

00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:47.910
Guess I'll have a drink, too.

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:50.130
Open up that wine.

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:52.220
Good idea. Misato-kun and 
Kawahama-kun brought it for me.

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:54.230
Don't! I'm scared!

00:12:54.230 --> 00:12:58.100
No! Just hope for a drunken 
Hasegawa confession!

00:12:58.800 --> 00:12:59.900
Did I hurt you?

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:01.140
A little.

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:02.800
Sorry.

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:05.050
Want something to eat?

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:07.050
Sure.

00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:26.820
Soy Sauce

00:13:21.220 --> 00:13:23.160
I'm tired. I'm sleepy.

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:25.580
But the soy sauce is waiting for me.

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:26.820
I have to stir it!

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:28.120
Hazuki!

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:29.130
Hazuki's here!

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:39.260
Whoa... Oikawa's covered in microbes...

00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:41.050
It's Microbe Monster No. 2!

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:51.520
Don't worry.

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:54.380
I only had one glass today.

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:55.680
Oh...

00:13:55.950 --> 00:13:58.290
It's been nothing but family meetings

00:13:58.290 --> 00:14:00.070
since I got back. I've had it.

00:14:00.070 --> 00:14:01.500
Even though Ryuuta-kun and I

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:04.690
both agreed to canceling 
the engagement ourselves...

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:08.050
So stuff like that really does happen.

00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:10.530
Well, anyway, at least it's over.

00:14:11.170 --> 00:14:15.170
Of course, now that I don't 
have to get married,

00:14:15.650 --> 00:14:19.380
I don't have a reason to stay 
at this school anymore.

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:20.290
Really?

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:22.090
Well, it's true.

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:24.720
I've stayed in the Itsuki 
seminar all this time

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:27.010
to escape from family obligations.

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:28.700
Oh...

00:14:28.700 --> 00:14:30.170
It's a little disappointing

00:14:30.170 --> 00:14:32.050
to hear you say it that way, though.

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:34.100
You're one to talk.

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:37.060
It's not like there's 
anything you want from me.

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:40.560
W-Well... I guess not...

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:47.070
The stars at the Route des 
Grand Crus were amazing.

00:14:48.190 --> 00:14:49.320
Yeah.

00:14:55.070 --> 00:14:56.800
A lot happened,

00:14:56.800 --> 00:14:59.830
but France turned out 
to be a great memory.

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:02.330
Thanks.

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:04.090
S-Sure.

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:06.920
I'm going to stop by the 
lab and then head home.

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:07.590
See you.

00:15:16.130 --> 00:15:19.220
A reason to stay here...

00:15:24.550 --> 00:15:25.580
Sawaki?

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:27.200
So it was you in here, Hasegawa-san.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:28.360
I saw the light on.

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:29.540
Yeah...

00:15:30.890 --> 00:15:31.860
What's that?

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:34.020
Messages from everyone.

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:35.230
Messages?

00:15:36.110 --> 00:15:39.270
Before we left for France 
to bring you back,

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:41.120
those who stayed here gave it to me.

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:43.470
What were they thinking...

00:15:43.470 --> 00:15:47.130
Well, everyone was sort 
of hyped up at the time.

00:15:47.850 --> 00:15:50.220
We ran a stall at the harvest festival

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:51.760
to raise money for plane tickets.

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:54.240
Misato-san and Kawahama-san even

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:57.030
donated the profits from 
their own sales to help.

00:15:57.990 --> 00:16:01.020
I didn't know any of that...

00:16:01.340 --> 00:16:04.020
Well, we did it because we wanted to.

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:22.000
It's really great that 
you're back, though.

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:25.630
It's been ages since everyone let 
loose like they did tonight.

00:16:27.510 --> 00:16:28.590
What is it?

00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:35.670
I don't have a reason 
to stay here anymore,

00:16:35.670 --> 00:16:38.640
but I guess I do have a 
reason to <i>want</i> to stay.

00:16:40.010 --> 00:16:40.780
Yep!

00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:43.120
Welcome back, Haruka!

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:44.630
Welcome back!

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:46.270
Hurry and look at us!

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:47.850
Look at us again!

00:16:47.850 --> 00:16:51.220
Hasegawa-san, the yeasts are thrilled.

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:55.010
They're saying "Welcome 
back!" and "Look at us!"

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:07.170
Since I work at home like this,

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:09.880
going out just means 
going to the vineyards

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:13.620
and I only occasionally go 
to Dijon, let alone Paris.

00:17:14.450 --> 00:17:19.770
But while I'm here, my wines 
are going out into the world.

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:23.180
That's why the wines 
are like my doubles.

00:17:24.010 --> 00:17:25.380
Just watch!

00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:28.690
Starting next year, my wine 
will captivate the world!

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:30.280
Shut up!

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:31.630
Think of how it feels 
to be your brother,

00:17:31.630 --> 00:17:33.190
being ordered around by you!

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:35.690
I had finally found a 
part-time job in Paris.

00:17:36.230 --> 00:17:38.200
Why were you in such 
a hurry to betray me?

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:40.550
Sorry.

00:17:41.340 --> 00:17:43.480
"Everyone work together," eh?

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:49.340
The message.

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:52.910
I've gotta let all those guys 
in Japan drink it soon, too!

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:02.140
That's from Marie?

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:03.300
Yeah.

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:05.560
So grapevines really do 
turn colors in fall.

00:18:05.990 --> 00:18:07.670
Awesome...

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:10.080
So which is it, Sawaki?

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:12.250
Yuuki or Marie?

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:14.190
Why are those my two choices?

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:16.390
Don't give us that!

00:18:16.390 --> 00:18:18.790
Whether it be Sawaki-kun's ability,

00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:22.770
or Yuuki-kun's cross-dressing,

00:18:22.770 --> 00:18:24.210
if you asked for their opinions

00:18:24.210 --> 00:18:25.920
on why they do what they do,

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:28.170
not everyone would be in agreement.

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:31.560
There are some fools out there 
who, even if they asked,

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:33.790
would only get angry and defiant if

00:18:33.790 --> 00:18:35.960
they weren't satisfied with the answer.

00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:40.520
Knowing everything won't 
necessarily bring happiness,

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:44.300
but if you give up trying 
to find out, it's all over.

00:18:45.050 --> 00:18:48.380
If the thing that interests 
you the most is here,

00:18:48.380 --> 00:18:51.750
you should stick to it diligently, 
and not try to rush.

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:01.450
Yes.

00:19:03.420 --> 00:19:05.520
Hey, it's Microbe Monster No. 2!

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:06.370
Oikawa?

00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:09.960
The microbes love her even more now...

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:11.520
All right, boys!

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:13.450
We're starting!

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:14.170
Wha?

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:14.960
Huh?

00:19:15.260 --> 00:19:17.210
Our leader rises again?

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:19.120
Come on, Mutou-san, you, too!

00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:21.470
Let's work hard to open 
up new frontiers!

00:19:21.830 --> 00:19:23.470
New frontiers, huh?

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:29.040
Sounds good to me! Let's do it!

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:32.270
Now that everyone's back, 
let's make some miso!

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:33.520
Yeah!

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:36.780
Yeah!

00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:38.620
Wow...

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:41.820
Let's start a batch of 
sake after the miso.

00:19:42.400 --> 00:19:43.320
Yeah!

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:46.820
Moyashimon is gonna keep on brewing!

00:19:47.690 --> 00:19:50.500
Well then, au revoir, everyone!

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:53.350
Je t'adore until we meet again!

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:31.020
Moyashimon

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:31.020
Returns

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:31.020
Episode 11

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:31.020
Microbe 
Theater

00:21:28.380 --> 00:21:31.020
Microbe Theater Returns!

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:31.020
Returns

00:21:31.730 --> 00:21:34.820
Microbe Theater Returns, 
which has continued

00:21:34.820 --> 00:21:36.850
until today thanks to 
all of your support...

00:21:37.260 --> 00:21:39.770
...has also reached its final episode!

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:41.460
What?!

00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:43.640
We microbes would like 
to thank you for...

00:21:43.640 --> 00:21:45.970
Nobody told me this was the end!

00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:45.700
Salmonella

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:47.530
P.   aeruginosa

00:21:45.970 --> 00:21:47.490
I refuse to accept this!

00:21:47.490 --> 00:21:49.100
Come on, calm down!

00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:50.830
Rhinovirus

00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:50.830
B.  longum

00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:50.830
R. sulfidophilum

00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:50.830
Methanogenic 
Bacteria

00:21:49.100 --> 00:21:51.370
Show more of us!

00:21:51.850 --> 00:21:52.930
It's hopeless.

00:21:53.640 --> 00:21:57.390
Uh, we microbes are still 
living freely today...

00:21:57.190 --> 00:21:59.040
L.   edodes

00:21:57.390 --> 00:21:58.490
Show me, too!

00:21:58.490 --> 00:21:59.950
Even if you can't see us...

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:01.550
B.   cinerea

00:22:01.060 --> 00:22:03.730
We're all around you 
and even inside you...

00:22:03.010 --> 00:22:04.720
T.   matsutake

00:22:03.730 --> 00:22:04.720
Me, too!

00:22:04.820 --> 00:22:07.380
So don't forget about us, okay?

00:22:08.160 --> 00:22:10.610
And now it's time to say goodbye.

00:22:10.610 --> 00:22:12.700
Though it saddens us to go...

00:22:12.700 --> 00:22:16.250
Well then, goodbye, everyone!

00:22:17.770 --> 00:22:19.890
But, allow us to be bold and say...

00:22:20.450 --> 00:22:22.480
I'll be back!

00:22:23.910 --> 00:22:25.930
We're gonna brew!

00:22:25.930 --> 00:22:27.990
See you next time!

00:22:28.010 --> 00:22:29.990
Hiyoshi Liquor Store

00:22:42.560 --> 00:22:43.960
Welcome.

00:22:43.960 --> 00:22:44.960
Kanou Farm

00:22:46.070 --> 00:22:49.970
To Be Continued

00:22:46.460 --> 00:22:47.970
To Be Continued...

00:22:47.970 --> 00:22:49.600
...maybe?

00:22:47.970 --> 00:22:49.970
maybe ?
